    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d163">

                <pb facs="0227" n="111" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg111"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.51/776.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Ambassador to Germany to the Secretary of
                        State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-02-28T13:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 28, 1912—1 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The German Government has reached our own conclusion that common action even in
                    the matter of finance is the wisest policy for the concerned powers to pursue
                    for the protection of the common interests in China, and consequently has
                    expressed its willingness to have Russia and Japan admitted into the financial
                    group.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Leishman.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
